  <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">MaterialByIsotropy</rdfs:label>
  <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A material is property-isotropic with respect to a given property if that property has the same value regardless of the direction in which you measure it. Isotropy is always property-specific: a material can be isotropic in one property and anisotropic in another simultaneously.</rdfs:comment>
  <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The class for materials categorised according to the isotropicity of their properties.</rdfs:comment>
  <core:prefLabel xml:lang="en">MaterialByIsotropy</core:prefLabel>
  <conceptualisation xml:lang="en">A material is property-isotropic with respect to a given property if that property has the same value regardless of the direction in which you measure it. Isotropy is always property-specific: a material can be isotropic in one property and anisotropic in another simultaneously.</conceptualisation>
  <elucidation xml:lang="en">The class for materials categorised according to the isotropicity of their properties.</elucidation>
</owl:Class>

