  <wikipediaReference rdf:resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Solution_(chemistry)"/>
  <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Solution</rdfs:label>
  <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A solution is a homogeneous mixture composed of two or more substances, when for convenience one (or more) substance, which is called the solvent, is treated differently from the other substances, which are called solutes.</rdfs:comment>
  <core:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Solution</core:prefLabel>
  <elucidation xml:lang="en">A solution is a homogeneous mixture composed of two or more substances, when for convenience one (or more) substance, which is called the solvent, is treated differently from the other substances, which are called solutes.</elucidation>
  <note xml:lang="en">IUPAC Goldbook definition is restricted to liquid or solid solutions. Here we extend the concept also to gas.</note>
  <note xml:lang="en">Solutions are characterized by the occurrence of Rayleigh scattering on light,</note>
</owl:Class>

