  <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="#EMMO_f2ca6dd0_0e5f_4392_a92d_cafdae6cfc95"/>
  <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">LuminousEfficacyOf540THzRadiation</rdfs:label>
  <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Defines the Candela base unit in the SI system.</rdfs:comment>
  <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The luminous efficacy of monochromatic radiation of frequency 540 × 10 12 Hz, K cd , is a technical constant that gives an exact numerical relationship between the purely physical characteristics of the radiant power stimulating the human eye (W) and its photobiological response defined by the luminous flux due to the spectral responsivity of a standard observer (lm) at a frequency of 540 × 10 12 hertz.</rdfs:comment>
  <core:prefLabel xml:lang="en">LuminousEfficacyOf540THzRadiation</core:prefLabel>
  <elucidation xml:lang="en">The luminous efficacy of monochromatic radiation of frequency 540 × 10 12 Hz, K cd , is a technical constant that gives an exact numerical relationship between the purely physical characteristics of the radiant power stimulating the human eye (W) and its photobiological response defined by the luminous flux due to the spectral responsivity of a standard observer (lm) at a frequency of 540 × 10 12 hertz.</elucidation>
</owl:Class>

