  <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">TaskTile</rdfs:label>
  <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A task that is a well formed tile of a workflow, according to a reductionistic description.</rdfs:comment>
  <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">While a task is only an holistic part of a workflow, a task tile provide a more precise context about the placement of a task in the topological structure of a workflow by using a reductionistic categorization. A workflow is now seen as a tiling and the task is on of its tiles.</rdfs:comment>
  <core:altLabel xml:lang="en">Step</core:altLabel>
  <core:prefLabel xml:lang="en">TaskTile</core:prefLabel>
  <conceptualisation xml:lang="en">While a task is only an holistic part of a workflow, a task tile provide a more precise context about the placement of a task in the topological structure of a workflow by using a reductionistic categorization. A workflow is now seen as a tiling and the task is on of its tiles.</conceptualisation>
  <elucidation xml:lang="en">A task that is a well formed tile of a workflow, according to a reductionistic description.</elucidation>
  <note xml:lang="en">A task tile is part of a specific granularity level for the workflow description, as composition of tasks.</note>
</owl:Class>

