  <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">PolymericMaterial</rdfs:label>
  <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A substance made of macromolecules formed by linking many smaller, repeating chemical units called monomers into long chains or networks, resulting in unique properties like toughness, elasticity, or flexibility, found in both natural forms (like DNA, protein) and synthetic plastics, rubbers, and fibers.</rdfs:comment>
  <core:example xml:lang="en">Nylon</core:example>
  <core:example xml:lang="en">PTFE</core:example>
  <core:example xml:lang="en">Poly Vinyl Chloride (PVC)</core:example>
  <core:example xml:lang="en">Polyethylene (PE)</core:example>
  <core:example xml:lang="en">Polystyrene (PS)</core:example>
  <core:example xml:lang="en">Rubber</core:example>
  <core:prefLabel xml:lang="en">PolymericMaterial</core:prefLabel>
  <elucidation xml:lang="en">A substance made of macromolecules formed by linking many smaller, repeating chemical units called monomers into long chains or networks, resulting in unique properties like toughness, elasticity, or flexibility, found in both natural forms (like DNA, protein) and synthetic plastics, rubbers, and fibers.</elucidation>
</owl:Class>

