  <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">SourceCode</rdfs:label>
  <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A programming language entity expressing a formal detailed plan of what a software is intended to do.</rdfs:comment>
  <core:prefLabel xml:lang="en">SourceCode</core:prefLabel>
  <elucidation xml:lang="en">A programming language entity expressing a formal detailed plan of what a software is intended to do.</elucidation>
  <note xml:lang="en">A source code is the companion of an application, being it the entity used to generate the application list of CPU executable instructions.</note>
  <note xml:lang="en">Source code (also referred to as source or code) is the version of software as it is originally written (i.e., typed into a computer) by a human in plain text (i.e., human readable alphanumeric characters).</note>
</owl:Class>

