  <EMMO_d088a3cb_d3e3_4eb2_9897_00aef0cb00cd rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double">0.0</EMMO_d088a3cb_d3e3_4eb2_9897_00aef0cb00cd>
  <EMMO_daf7a9b7_18ef_4e73_9fb9_75adfd9800e8 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Ban</EMMO_daf7a9b7_18ef_4e73_9fb9_75adfd9800e8>
  <elucidation xml:lang="en">A ban is a logarithmic unit which measures information or entropy, based on base 10 logarithms and powers of 10, rather than the powers of 2 and base 2 logarithms which define the bit. One ban is approximately 3.32 (log₂ 10) bits.

-- QUDT</elucidation>
