  <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">AmperePerMetre</rdfs:label>
  <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en"> is the SI unit of magnetic field strength. One ampere per meter is equal to π/250 oersteds (12.566  371 millioersteds) in CGS units. The ampere per meter is also the SI unit of "magnetization" in the sense of magnetic dipole moment per unit volume; in this context 1 A/m = 0.001 emu per cubic centimeter.

-- QUDT</rdfs:comment>
  <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">http://qudt.org/2.1/vocab/unit</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
  <core:altLabel xml:lang="en">Ampere per Metre</core:altLabel>
  <core:prefLabel xml:lang="en">AmperePerMetre</core:prefLabel>
  <EMMO_8189b42e_0995_423a_a26c_51168b27c3cf rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double">1.0</EMMO_8189b42e_0995_423a_a26c_51168b27c3cf>
  <EMMO_d088a3cb_d3e3_4eb2_9897_00aef0cb00cd rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double">0.0</EMMO_d088a3cb_d3e3_4eb2_9897_00aef0cb00cd>
  <elucidation xml:lang="en"> is the SI unit of magnetic field strength. One ampere per meter is equal to π/250 oersteds (12.566  371 millioersteds) in CGS units. The ampere per meter is also the SI unit of "magnetization" in the sense of magnetic dipole moment per unit volume; in this context 1 A/m = 0.001 emu per cubic centimeter.

-- QUDT</elucidation>
  <qudtReference rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/A-PER-M</qudtReference>
  <ucumCode rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">A.m-1</ucumCode>
  <ucumCode rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">A/m</ucumCode>
  <unitSymbol rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">A/m</unitSymbol>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

