<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Degree">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#EMMO_6795a4b8_ffd0_4588_a581_a9413fe49cac"/>
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#EMMO_cdc962d8_f3ea_4764_a57a_c7caa4859179"/>
  <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/emmo/disciplines/units/siacceptedspecialunits-abox#"/>
  <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Degree</rdfs:label>
  <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A degree (in full, a degree of arc, arc degree, or arcdegree), usually denoted by ° (the degree symbol), is a measurement of plane angle, representing 1/360 of a full rotation; one degree is equivalent to  2π /360 rad, 0.017453 rad. It is not an SI unit, as the SI unit for angles is radian, but is an accepted SI unit.

-- QUDT</rdfs:comment>
  <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Degree is a measurement of plane angle, defined by representing a full rotation as 360 degrees.</rdfs:comment>
  <core:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Degree</core:prefLabel>
  <sche:unitCode rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">DD</sche:unitCode>
  <EMMO_8189b42e_0995_423a_a26c_51168b27c3cf rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double">0.01745329</EMMO_8189b42e_0995_423a_a26c_51168b27c3cf>
  <EMMO_d088a3cb_d3e3_4eb2_9897_00aef0cb00cd rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double">0.0</EMMO_d088a3cb_d3e3_4eb2_9897_00aef0cb00cd>
  <EMMO_daf7a9b7_18ef_4e73_9fb9_75adfd9800e8 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">°</EMMO_daf7a9b7_18ef_4e73_9fb9_75adfd9800e8>
  <dbpediaReference rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">http://dbpedia.org/page/Degree_(angle)</dbpediaReference>
  <definition xml:lang="en">Degree is a measurement of plane angle, defined by representing a full rotation as 360 degrees.</definition>
  <elucidation xml:lang="en">A degree (in full, a degree of arc, arc degree, or arcdegree), usually denoted by ° (the degree symbol), is a measurement of plane angle, representing 1/360 of a full rotation; one degree is equivalent to  2π /360 rad, 0.017453 rad. It is not an SI unit, as the SI unit for angles is radian, but is an accepted SI unit.

-- QUDT</elucidation>
  <iupacReference rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">https://doi.org/10.1351/goldbook.D01560</iupacReference>
  <qudtReference rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/DEG</qudtReference>
  <ucumCode rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">deg</ucumCode>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

