<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Arcsecond">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#EMMO_6795a4b8_ffd0_4588_a581_a9413fe49cac"/>
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#EMMO_868ae137_4d25_493e_b270_21ea3d94849e"/>
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#EMMO_cdc962d8_f3ea_4764_a57a_c7caa4859179"/>
  <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/emmo/disciplines/units/siacceptedspecialunits-abox#"/>
  <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Arcsecond</rdfs:label>
  <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">"Arc Second" is a unit of angular measure, also called the `second of arc`, equal to 1/60 arcminute. One arcsecond is a very small angle: there are 1,296,000 in a circle. The SI recommends `double prime` ('') as the symbol for the arcsecond. The symbol has become common in astronomy, where very small angles are stated in milliarcseconds (mas).

-- QUDT</rdfs:comment>
  <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">http://qudt.org/2.1/vocab/unit</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
  <core:altLabel xml:lang="en">ArcSecond</core:altLabel>
  <core:altLabel xml:lang="en">SecondOfArc</core:altLabel>
