  <elucidation xml:lang="en">Joule Per Square Meter (J/m²) is a unit in the category of Energy density. It is also known as joules per square meter, joule per square metre, joule/square meter, joule/square metre. This unit is commonly used in the SI unit system.

-- QUDT</elucidation>
  <qudtReference rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/J-PER-M2</qudtReference>
  <ucumCode rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">J.m-2</ucumCode>
  <ucumCode rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">J/m2</ucumCode>
  <unitSymbol rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">J/m²</unitSymbol>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

