  <definition xml:lang="en">The ampere, symbol A, is the SI unit of electric current. It is defined by taking the fixed numerical value of the elementary charge e to be 1.602176634×10−19 when expressed in the unit C, which is equal to A s, where the second is defined in terms of ∆νCs.</definition>
  <iupacReference rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">https://doi.org/10.1351/goldbook.A00300</iupacReference>
  <qudtReference rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/A</qudtReference>
  <ucumCode rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">A</ucumCode>
  <wikipediaReference rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI">http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ampere?oldid=494026699</wikipediaReference>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

