<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#Hartree">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#EMMO_868ae137_4d25_493e_b270_21ea3d94849e"/>
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#EMMO_f0404eb3_433e_48af_a50f_67f1a03f5f0c"/>
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#EMMO_f6070071_d054_4b17_9d2d_f446f7147d0f"/>
  <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/emmo/disciplines/units/specialunits-abox#"/>
  <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Hartree</rdfs:label>
  <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The `Hartree` (symbol: E_h or Ha), also known as the `Hartree Energy`, is the atomic unit of energy. The hartree energy is equal to the absolute value of the electric potential energy of the hydrogen atom in its ground state. The energy of the electron in an H-atom in its ground state is -E_H, where E_H= 2 R_∞ · hc₀. The 2006 CODATA recommended value was E_H = 4.35974394(22) × 10⁻¹⁸ J = 27.21138386(68) eV.
Definition:
E_H = e²/(4π ε₀ a₀)
where, e is the elementary charge, ε₀ is the electric constant, and a₀ is the Bohr radius.'

-- QUDT</rdfs:comment>
  <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">http://qudt.org/2.1/vocab/unit</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
  <core:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Hartree</core:prefLabel>
  <EMMO_8189b42e_0995_423a_a26c_51168b27c3cf rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double">4.359744e-18</EMMO_8189b42e_0995_423a_a26c_51168b27c3cf>
  <EMMO_d088a3cb_d3e3_4eb2_9897_00aef0cb00cd rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double">0.0</EMMO_d088a3cb_d3e3_4eb2_9897_00aef0cb00cd>
  <elucidation xml:lang="en">The `Hartree` (symbol: E_h or Ha), also known as the `Hartree Energy`, is the atomic unit of energy. The hartree energy is equal to the absolute value of the electric potential energy of the hydrogen atom in its ground state. The energy of the electron in an H-atom in its ground state is -E_H, where E_H= 2 R_∞ · hc₀. The 2006 CODATA recommended value was E_H = 4.35974394(22) × 10⁻¹⁸ J = 27.21138386(68) eV.
Definition:
E_H = e²/(4π ε₀ a₀)
where, e is the elementary charge, ε₀ is the electric constant, and a₀ is the Bohr radius.'

-- QUDT</elucidation>
  <qudtReference rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/E_h</qudtReference>
  <unitSymbol rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Ha</unitSymbol>
  <wikipediaReference rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hartree?oldid=489318053</wikipediaReference>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

