  <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Foot</rdfs:label>
  <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A foot is a unit of length defined as being 0.3048 m exactly and used in the imperial system of units and United States customary units. It is subdivided into 12 inches. The foot is still officially used in Canada and still commonly used in the United Kingdom, although the latter has partially metricated its units of measurement.

-- QUDT</rdfs:comment>
  <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">http://qudt.org/2.1/vocab/unit</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
  <core:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Foot</core:prefLabel>
  <EMMO_8189b42e_0995_423a_a26c_51168b27c3cf rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double">0.3048</EMMO_8189b42e_0995_423a_a26c_51168b27c3cf>
  <EMMO_d088a3cb_d3e3_4eb2_9897_00aef0cb00cd rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double">0.0</EMMO_d088a3cb_d3e3_4eb2_9897_00aef0cb00cd>
  <elucidation xml:lang="en">A foot is a unit of length defined as being 0.3048 m exactly and used in the imperial system of units and United States customary units. It is subdivided into 12 inches. The foot is still officially used in Canada and still commonly used in the United Kingdom, although the latter has partially metricated its units of measurement.

-- QUDT</elucidation>
  <qudtReference rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/FT</qudtReference>
