  <EMMO_d088a3cb_d3e3_4eb2_9897_00aef0cb00cd rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double">0.0</EMMO_d088a3cb_d3e3_4eb2_9897_00aef0cb00cd>
  <elucidation xml:lang="en">The fundamental unit of magnetomotive force (mmf) in electromagnetic units is called a Gilbert. It is the mmf which will produce a magnetic field strength of one Gauss (Maxwell per Square Centimeter) in a path one centimeter long.

-- QUDT</elucidation>
  <qudtReference rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/GI</qudtReference>
