  <EMMO_8189b42e_0995_423a_a26c_51168b27c3cf rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double">0.0254</EMMO_8189b42e_0995_423a_a26c_51168b27c3cf>
  <EMMO_d088a3cb_d3e3_4eb2_9897_00aef0cb00cd rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double">0.0</EMMO_d088a3cb_d3e3_4eb2_9897_00aef0cb00cd>
  <elucidation xml:lang="en">An inch is the name of a unit of length in a number of different systems, including Imperial units, and United States customary units. There are 36 inches in a yard and 12 inches in a foot. Corresponding units of area and volume are the square inch and the cubic inch.

-- QUDT</elucidation>
  <qudtReference rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/IN</qudtReference>
