<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="#MilliArcsecond">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#EMMO_8246541a_f1f6_4d03_8bd7_fc6b76d17375"/>
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#EMMO_a3a701ed_6f7d_4a10_9aee_dfa1961fc7b7"/>
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#EMMO_c6d4a5e0_7e95_44df_a6db_84ee0a8bbc8e"/>
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="#EMMO_cdc962d8_f3ea_4764_a57a_c7caa4859179"/>
  <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/emmo/disciplines/units/siacceptedunits-abox#"/>
  <EMMO_d4e0a0ab_2f67_4f87_a0db_b544e6dceed4 rdf:resource="#Arcsecond"/>
  <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">MilliArcsecond</rdfs:label>
  <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A minute of arc, arcminute, or minute arc (MOA), is a unit of angular measurement equal to one sixtieth (1/60) of one degree (circle/21,600), or π /10,800 radians. In turn, a second of arc or arcsecond is one sixtieth (1/60) of one minute of arc. Since one degree is defined as one three hundred and sixtieth (1/360) of a rotation, one minute of arc is 1/21,600 of a rotation.  the milliarcsecond, abbreviated mas, is used in astronomy.

-- QUDT</rdfs:comment>
  <core:altLabel xml:lang="en">Milli ArcSecond</core:altLabel>
  <core:prefLabel xml:lang="en">MilliArcsecond</core:prefLabel>
  <EMMO_8189b42e_0995_423a_a26c_51168b27c3cf rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double">4.848137e-09</EMMO_8189b42e_0995_423a_a26c_51168b27c3cf>
  <EMMO_d088a3cb_d3e3_4eb2_9897_00aef0cb00cd rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double">0.0</EMMO_d088a3cb_d3e3_4eb2_9897_00aef0cb00cd>
  <elucidation xml:lang="en">A minute of arc, arcminute, or minute arc (MOA), is a unit of angular measurement equal to one sixtieth (1/60) of one degree (circle/21,600), or π /10,800 radians. In turn, a second of arc or arcsecond is one sixtieth (1/60) of one minute of arc. Since one degree is defined as one three hundred and sixtieth (1/360) of a rotation, one minute of arc is 1/21,600 of a rotation.  the milliarcsecond, abbreviated mas, is used in astronomy.

-- QUDT</elucidation>
  <qudtReference rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliARCSEC</qudtReference>
  <ucumCode rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">m''</ucumCode>
  <unitSymbol rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">mas</unitSymbol>
  <wikipediaReference rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Minute_of_arc</wikipediaReference>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

