<owl:AsymmetricProperty rdf:about="#EMMO_67fc0a36_8dcb_4ffa_9a43_31074efa3296">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#InverseFunctionalProperty"/>
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#IrreflexiveProperty"/>
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
  <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="#EMMO_0650c031_42b6_4f0a_b62d_d88f071da6bf"/>
  <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/emmo/disciplines/metrology#"/>
  <rdfs:range rdf:resource="#EMMO_18ce5200_00f5_45bb_8c6f_6fb128cd41ae"/>
  <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="#EMMO_55375713_8f92_473b_a688_b7fcc14f7797"/>
  <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">hasMetrologicalReference</rdfs:label>
  <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Relates a quantity to its metrological reference through a semiotic process.</rdfs:comment>
  <owl:versionInfo rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">In EMMO version 1.0.0, physical quantities used the hasMetrologicalReference object property to relate them to their units via physical dimensionality. This was simplified in 1.0.0-alpha3 in order to make reasoning faster.

The restriction (e.g. for the physical quantity Length)

    Length hasMetrologicalReference only (hasPhysicsDimension only LengthDimension)

was in 1.0.0-alpha3 changed to

    Length hasPhysicsDimension some LengthDimension

Likewise were the universal restrictions on the corresponding unit changed to excistential. E.g.

    Metre hasPhysicsDimension only LengthDimension

was changed to

    Metre hasPhysicsDimension some LengthDimension

The label of this class was also changed from PhysicsDimension to PhysicalDimension.</owl:versionInfo>
  <core:prefLabel xml:lang="en">hasMetrologicalReference</core:prefLabel>
</owl:AsymmetricProperty>

